# Platform shared (PWA + Windows)

GIS Toolbox has **one shared React/MapLibre frontend** used by:

1. The public progressive web app
2. A private Windows 11 desktop application (Tauri / WebView2 — when present)

## Default all work to shared code

- Widgets, map, tools, UI, and bug fixes go in `js/` and `react/`
- Shared widgets remain in `js/widgets/` and `react/widgets/`
- **Never** create Windows copies of shared widgets
- Widget engines must remain platform-independent (no DOM/Tauri/Python imports)

## Platform behavior

- Inject platform APIs through `WidgetContext` (`ctx.platform`, `ctx.services`)
- Contracts live in `js/platform/contracts.js`
- Web provider: `js/platform/web/`
- Windows provider (when added): `js/platform/windows/` only

## Hard rules

- Do **not** directly import `@tauri-apps/*` outside `js/platform/windows/`
- Do **not** import Python/sidecar code into shared application modules
- Use registry `requiredCapabilities` / `optionalCapabilities` instead of scattered `if (desktop)` checks
- After shared changes, both `npm run build` (or `build:web`) and `npm run build:desktop` must stay green
